# A content-addressed delta's retirement/suppression rows for the diamond EDB: retire
# the DIRECT shortcut edge a -> c. Plain Turtle triples (default graph); the
# `gmeow logic session` loader re-homes them into the single session world exactly as
# the additions are, so the committed delta carries a NON-EMPTY suppression.
#
# After this retraction the height-1 direct proof of `reach(a, c)` is gone, but
# `reach(a, c)` SURVIVES via the transitive path a -> b -> c, so its maintained
# min-proof-height RISES 1 -> 2. This is the CLI-observable witness for AC2's
# "a retract RAISES a surviving fact's proof height".
@prefix ex: <https://example.org/session/> .

ex:a ex:edge ex:c .
